// RUN: cd %corpus && ! %zomc compile --check 09-interfaces/impl_trait_method_body_capability_neg_49.zom > %t 2>&1
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file %t

// A concrete trait method supplied by a standalone impl block is not in the
// lowered surface yet (empty impls and `type Item = T` assignments are). A body
// that reads a receiver field into a local and returns the local has no shape,
// so the body checker drains it as ZOM4099 rather than an internal compiler
// error. The single `return this.<field>;` shape is covered by the
// impl-receiver-field native fixture instead.

// CHECK-LITERAL: Error [ZOM4099]: this function body uses a construct the compiler cannot generate code for yet
// CHECK-LITERAL:   --> conformance/09-interfaces/impl_trait_method_body_capability_neg_49.zom:10:16
